I return to my quiet flat.
I keep my medicines on the table.
I am tired.
I drink warm water and take the first tablet.
Just then, someone knocks on the door.
I open the door.
My neighbour Asha is standing outside.
Her dog, Moti, is also with her.
Asha asks, "Maya, how are you feeling now?"
I say, "I am not feeling well, Asha."
"I have a bad cold and my throat is also hurting."
Moti looks at me and wags his tail.
I smile and say, "Come here Moti, how are you?"
Asha says with concern, "Maya, you should rest now."
"You should eat light food and sleep peacefully."
I say to her, "Yes, definitely."
"Thank you so much, Asha."
Asha and Moti go back to their flat.
I close the door.
I finally get into bed and go to sleep.
